Quick viva revision
•	Greedy method: makes the best available local choice at each step.
•	Dynamic programming: stores results of smaller subproblems to avoid repeated work.
•	Backtracking: tries a choice; if it fails, it goes back and tries another choice.
•	KNN: classifies a sample using the labels of its nearest K training samples.
•	SVM: finds a decision boundary (hyperplane) that separates classes.
•	Neural network: learns patterns through connected layers of artificial neurons.
•	Confusion matrix: table showing correct and incorrect classification results.
•	Thread: a smaller execution path within a process; Python threads may not speed up CPU-heavy code.
